t, or what you will drink; nor yet for your body, what you will wear. Isn’t life more…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Mark 2:26","note":"How he entered into God’s house at the time of Abiathar the high priest, and ate the show bread, which is not lawful to eat except for the priests, and gave…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 4:2","note":"for forty days, being tempted by the devil. He ate nothing in those days. Afterward, when they were completed, he was hungry.","source":"web"},{"ref":"John 4:31","note":"In the meanwhile, the disciples urged him, saying, “Rabbi, eat.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 9:9","note":"He was without sight for three days, and neither ate nor drank.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Romans 14:2","note":"One man has faith to eat all things, but he who is weak eats only vegetables.","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 8:8","note":"But food will not commend us to God. For neither, if we don’t eat, are we the worse; nor, if we eat, are we the better.","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Thessalonians 3:8","note":"neither did we eat bread from anyone’s hand without paying for it, but in labor and travail worked night and day, that we might not burden any of you,","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G2068","lemma":"ἐσθίω","transliteration":"esthiō","gloss":"to eat"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}